stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> REPORTED : Employee reports incident (initial state)

    REPORTED --> ASSIGNED : Technician assigned (manual / strategy, capacity permitting)
    REPORTED --> CANCELLED : Reporter or Admin cancels ticket

    ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : Assignee acknowledges (meets response target)
    ASSIGNED --> IN_PROGRESS : Technician starts work straight away (counts as acknowledging)
    ASSIGNED --> ASSIGNED : Admin reassigns (or L2 escalation auto-reassigns)
    ASSIGNED --> CANCELLED : Admin cancels ticket

    ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : Technician starts diagnosis / work
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> ASSIGNED : Reassigned (new technician must accept it)
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> CANCELLED : Admin cancels ticket

    state IN_PROGRESS {
        [*] --> Diagnosing
        Diagnosing --> Remediating
        Remediating --> Testing
    }

    IN_PROGRESS --> PENDING_INFO : Technician requests clarification (pauses SLA)
    PENDING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : Reporter provides requested info (resumes SLA)

    IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : Technician provides resolution summary
    IN_PROGRESS --> ASSIGNED : Reassigned to different tier / specialist

    REPORTED --> RESOLVED : resolveWithParent (major incident resolved)
    ASSIGNED --> RESOLVED : resolveWithParent (major incident resolved)
    ACKNOWLEDGED --> RESOLVED : resolveWithParent (major incident resolved)
    IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolveWithParent (major incident resolved)
    PENDING_INFO --> RESOLVED : resolveWithParent (resumes SLA clock first)

    RESOLVED --> CLOSED : Reporter verifies and accepts resolution
    RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : Reporter or Admin rejects resolution (reason required)
    RESOLVED --> CLOSED : System auto-closes after 48h inactivity

    CLOSED --> IN_PROGRESS : Reporter or Admin reopens within 14 days (reason required)
    CLOSED --> [*] : Reopen window expired
    CANCELLED --> [*] : Terminal state (immutable)

    note right of PENDING_INFO
        SLA resolution clock is PAUSED while waiting for user info.
        Resumes immediately upon user submission.
    end note

    note right of ACKNOWLEDGED
        Accepted but not started. respondedAt is set,
        so the ticket no longer escalates for response.
    end note

    note left of CLOSED
        FORBIDDEN TRANSITIONS:
        - CLOSED -> Any state except IN_PROGRESS within 14 days
        - CANCELLED -> Any state (strictly immutable)
        - REPORTED -> RESOLVED / CLOSED (must pass through IN_PROGRESS,
          except resolveWithParent for tickets linked to a major incident)
        - ASSIGNED / ACKNOWLEDGED -> CLOSED (must be resolved first)
        - PENDING_INFO -> RESOLVED (must return to IN_PROGRESS first,
          except resolveWithParent)
        - IN_PROGRESS / PENDING_INFO -> CANCELLED
    end note
